          <li class="border-t py-3.5"><span class="text-foreground">Notarised macOS builds.</span> Releases are ad-hoc signed; Developer ID signing and notarisation are planned.</li>
          <li class="border-t py-3.5"><span class="text-foreground">In-app updates.</span> To update, run the install command again.</li>
          <li class="border-t py-3.5"><span class="text-foreground">PDF, video, audio and slides.</span> Planned as primitives; today an agent says it can't show a PDF.</li>
          <li class="border-t py-3.5"><span class="text-foreground">Interactive widgets.</span> A sandboxed node that speaks the MCP Apps protocol is being considered.</li>
          <li class="border-t py-3.5"><span class="text-foreground">A public library index.</span> Libraries install from any git URL; there's no shared catalogue.</li>
